            <h2>Crop to Fit vs. Fit Without Cropping: Which Mode Should You Choose?</h2>
            <p>
              When you <strong>change photo ratio online</strong>, there are two primary methods for converting an image from its source proportions to a new aspect ratio:
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Crop to Fit (Fill Canvas):</strong> This method expands the image until it completely fills the dimensions of the target aspect ratio. Any parts of the image that extend beyond the new boundary are trimmed away. This is the optimal choice when you want a clean, edge-to-edge full-bleed look and your subject has sufficient breathing room around the edges. Our interactive stage lets you drag and pan the image smoothly to reposition the focal point.</li>
              <li><strong>Fit Without Cropping (Letterbox / Pillarbox):</strong> This method scales the image so that 100% of the original photo remains completely visible within the new frame. Because the source ratio differs from the target ratio, extra space appears around the photo (letterboxing on top and bottom, or pillarboxing on the left and right). You can fill these margins with clean solid colors (white, black, dark slate), transparent alpha pixels (for PNG and WebP), or an aesthetically pleasing blurred reflection of your photo.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Standard Social Media Aspect Ratios Reference (2026 Guide)</h2>
            <p>
              Every major social platform recommends specific aspect ratios to maximize visual engagement and prevent compression artifacts in mobile feeds:
            </p>

            <div class="table-responsive-wrapper">
              <table class="content-table">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>Aspect Ratio</th>
                    <th>Orientation</th>
                    <th>Standard Resolution (px)</th>
                    <th>Primary Platforms &amp; Content Formats</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td><strong>1:1</strong></td>
                    <td>Square</td>
                    <td>1080 × 1080, 1200 × 1200</td>
                    <td>Instagram Feed Posts, Profile Pictures, Facebook Ads, Product Thumbnails</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><strong>4:5</strong></td>
                    <td>Vertical Portrait</td>
                    <td>1080 × 1350</td>
                    <td>Instagram Vertical Feed (Captures Maximum Mobile Screen Real Estate)</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><strong>9:16</strong></td>
                    <td>Full Vertical</td>
                    <td>1080 × 1920, 720 × 1280</td>
                    <td>TikTok Videos, Instagram Reels, YouTube Shorts, Snapchat &amp; Facebook Stories</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><strong>16:9</strong></td>
                    <td>Widescreen (Landscape)</td>
